---
description: Put heading subtitles / helper copy in an info icon beside the heading
alwaysApply: true
---

# Heading details → info icon

Do **not** place a subtitle, description, or helper line under page/section headings as always-visible body text when that copy only explains the heading.

## Pattern

1. Keep the **heading** (and badges / counts if needed) on one row.
2. Put the explanatory copy in an **info** (`Info` from `lucide-react`) control **beside** the heading.
3. On click/tap, show a small popover (same pattern as Transactions / `/newentry` / Documents).
4. Apply on **mobile and desktop** unless the user explicitly asks for a visible subtitle.

## Do

```tsx
<div className="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2">
  <h1 className="truncate text-2xl font-bold …">Add Transaction</h1>
  <div className="relative shrink-0">
    <button type="button" aria-label="About …" aria-expanded={infoOpen} …>
      <Info className="h-5 w-5" aria-hidden />
    </button>
    {infoOpen ? (
      <>
        <div className="fixed inset-0 z-40" onClick={() => setInfoOpen(false)} aria-hidden />
        <div role="dialog" className="absolute … z-50 …">
          Create a ledger entry or transfer between accounts.
        </div>
      </>
    ) : null}
  </div>
</div>
```

## Do not

- Leave a permanent `mt-1 text-sm text-gray-500` subtitle under the title when an info popover would do.
- Duplicate the same hint both under the heading **and** inside the section body (e.g. Documents) — prefer one info icon on the heading and `hideHint` / no inline helper.

## Scope

Page titles, section titles (Details / Documents / settings rows that act as headings), and similar UI chrome across `app/` and `demo-mode/`.
